From dbf730e05e8e25d63ff3be03accd515b0e74cd17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Shields <noisyoly@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:42:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Server: plan-only jobs, per-half adapter strengths,
 timestep-embedding adapters

POST /plan runs the first stage alone, under the planner half of the request's
adapters, and returns the score with the seed it was drawn with: a front end
can let the score be read and edited before anything is rendered.

An adapter in a request can set scale_ar and scale_nar apart: a style adapter's
planner half and acoustic half are often wanted at different strengths, and a
voice adapter on the acoustic half alone.  scale still covers a half not named.

Adapters that also train the acoustic half's timestep embedding
(time_embedder.mlp.0 and .2) were skipped at the scan as unsupported; they
merge like vae2llm and llm2vae.

POST /adapters/rescan reads the adapter directory again, from the worker,
so a file added after the start can be named without a restart.  /props
reports the compute device and its free and total memory.
